From 02a06a1ce7096780ea6dd19278fcd95cae971816 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: juansolo457 <5344231+Juansolo457@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:51:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Aim assist: the Xbox 360 muzzle aim (pm_AimAssist 2)

Recovered from the 360 executable's rvWeapon::Attack (default.xex 0x8250D670):
while the aim assist has a target and the view ray (MASK_SHOT_RENDERMODEL, out to
pm_AimAssistDistance) does not already hit it, each shot leaves the muzzle toward
the target's joint with the smallest angle from that ray (0x824421A0), or its
origin raised 32 units when no joint lies ahead. A teammate under the crosshair
is never shot past; the shot goes to the crosshair point. pm_AimAssistBump and
pm_AimAssistThreshold are unused on the 360 too.

The 360 applied it for every input and in multiplayer; here it is single player
and controller only (pm_AimAssistAnyInput, a cheat, lifts that for testing).

- rvWeapon::XenonMuzzleAim, called from Attack; GetAutoAimFOV reads the weapon
  def's aimAssistFOV, the key the 360 uses.
- Settings > Controller > Aim Assist: No / Slowdown Only (1) / Full (360) (2).
- testMuzzleAim (cheat): prints how a shot fired now would be turned;
  "testMuzzleAim aim" turns the view there. pm_showAimAssist 1 names the joint
  and draws the corrected shot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
